NAME
       cd - change the working directory

SYNOPSIS
       cd [DIRECTORY]

DESCRIPTION
       cd is a shell built-in: it changes the current directory of the shell.
       Without DIRECTORY it goes to $HOME; cd - returns to the previous
       directory. /bin/cd only checks that DIRECTORY exists, because a separate
       program cannot change the directory of its parent.

EXAMPLES
       cd /usr/share/man
       cd ..
       cd

SEE ALSO
       pwd(1), sh(1)
